+# amber-user-website Agent Notes
+
+This repository includes an in-repo LLM wiki scaffold under `.llm-wiki/`.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Use the wiki to accumulate stable project knowledge without mixing generated notes into product code.
+
+## Wiki layout
+
+- `.llm-wiki/raw/` contains immutable source inputs such as copied specs, command transcripts, screenshots, and investigation notes.
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/` contains LLM-maintained markdown pages that summarize the codebase and connect concepts.
+- `.llm-wiki/schema/` defines how wiki pages should be written and updated.
+
+## Working rules
+
+- Treat product code as the source of truth for implementation details.
+- Treat `.llm-wiki/raw/` as append-only unless a duplicate or mistake is being corrected.
+- Prefer updating existing wiki pages over creating near-duplicate pages.
+- Record uncertainty explicitly instead of guessing.
+- When a page cites code, include repo-relative file paths and enough context to relocate the source quickly.
+
+## Good workflow
+
+1. Read the relevant code or docs.
+2. If the input is external or ephemeral, snapshot it into `.llm-wiki/raw/`.
+3. Update one or more pages in `.llm-wiki/wiki/`.
+4. Keep page summaries short, factual, and cross-linked.
+
+## Current seed pages
+
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/Overview.md`
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/Architecture.md`
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/Routes-and-Areas.md`
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/Operations.md`
+- `.llm-wiki/wiki/Open-Questions.md`
