+# LLM Wiki Workspace
+
+This directory is a lightweight, repo-local version of the LLM Wiki pattern for `amber-user-website`.
+
+## Goal
+
+Keep code understanding, architecture notes, and future investigation work in one place without polluting the app source tree.
+
+## Structure
+
+- `raw/`
+  Immutable inputs for the wiki. Put copied tickets, product notes, command outputs, screenshots, and one-off investigation artifacts here.
+- `wiki/`
+  LLM-maintained knowledge pages. These pages should summarize what the repo does today and link to related pages instead of duplicating content.
+- `schema/`
+  Rules for page naming, page structure, citations, and update behavior.
+
+## Suggested usage
+
+1. Add or capture source material in `raw/` when the information does not already live in the repo.
+2. Read the matching code paths in `src/`, `webpack/`, and `scripts/`.
+3. Update the relevant pages in `wiki/`.
+4. Add follow-up questions to `wiki/Open-Questions.md` instead of leaving them in chat history only.
+
+## What belongs here
+
+- Route maps
+- Architecture summaries
+- Operational runbooks
+- Integration notes
+- Known risks and open questions
+
+## What does not belong here
+
+- Generated build output
+- Private credentials
+- Large binary assets
+- Duplicated copies of source files when a link or citation is enough
+
+Start with:
+
+- `wiki/Overview.md`
+- `wiki/Architecture.md`
+- `wiki/Routes-and-Areas.md`
+- `wiki/Operations.md`
