+# Wiki Schema
+
+Use these conventions when creating or updating pages in `.llm-wiki/wiki/`.
+
+## Page template
+
+Every page should prefer this shape:
+
+1. `# Title`
+2. `## Summary`
+3. `## Key facts`
+4. `## Evidence`
+5. `## Related pages`
+6. `## Open questions` when needed
+
+## Writing rules
+
+- Prefer short factual paragraphs over long narrative dumps.
+- Prefer stable file paths like `src/routes/index.ts` over line numbers that drift quickly.
+- Call out environment-specific behavior when it changes for China, desktop, or whitelabel builds.
+- Separate facts from assumptions.
+- Update an existing page when the topic already exists.
+
+## Evidence rules
+
+When possible, back statements with one of:
+
+- Repo files
+- Commands that can be rerun locally
+- Captured artifacts in `.llm-wiki/raw/`
+
+Use a compact citation format:
+
+- `Code: src/routes/index.ts`
+- `Code: src/server/index.ts`
+- `Artifact: .llm-wiki/raw/<name>.md`
+
+## Page naming
+
+- Use `Pascal-Case.md` for wiki pages.
+- Keep names broad enough to survive refactors.
+- Prefer one durable page over multiple tiny pages.
+
+## Update policy
+
+- Do not rewrite the whole wiki for a small change.
+- Touch only the pages affected by the new information.
+- Add a brief note to `Open-Questions.md` when evidence is incomplete.
+
+## Seed topic map
+
+The current seed structure is:
+
+- `Overview.md`
+- `Architecture.md`
+- `Routes-and-Areas.md`
+- `Operations.md`
+- `Open-Questions.md`
+
+Add new pages only when a topic grows beyond a short section in one of the seed pages.
