+# Overview
+
+## Summary
+
+`amber-user-website` is a React 17 plus Express universal web application with server-side rendering, route-level data loading, and multiple runtime variants including default, desktop, China, and whitelabel modes.
+
+## Key facts
+
+- The project uses a custom SSR stack rather than Next.js.
+- Client and server bundles are built with Webpack.
+- Routing is defined centrally and supports language-prefixed paths for several areas.
+- Development and test workflows already exist through Yarn scripts.
+- The repository contains both customer-facing marketing flows and authenticated user flows.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Code: package.json
+- Code: src/routes/index.ts
+- Code: src/server/index.ts
+- Code: webpack/server.config.ts
+
+## Notable product areas
+
+- Discovery flows such as home, search, and property pages
+- Conversion flows such as book form, application, and payment
+- Account flows such as profile, bookings, offers, and activity
+- Content flows such as blog, news, podcast, exams, and media mentions
+- Brand and campaign pages such as about, ambassador, scholarship, and referral
+
+## Development entry points
+
+- `yarn dev`
+- `yarn dev-desktop`
+- `yarn test`
+- `yarn lint`
+
+## Related pages
+
+- [Architecture](./Architecture.md)
+- [Routes and Areas](./Routes-and-Areas.md)
+- [Operations](./Operations.md)
+- [Open Questions](./Open-Questions.md)
