+# Architecture
+
+## Summary
+
+The app is a custom universal React application. Express owns request handling, middleware, static asset serving, proxy endpoints, and SSR orchestration.
+
+## Key facts
+
+- The server boots from `src/server/index.ts`.
+- SSR logic lives under `src/server/`, including HTML rendering and request handling.
+- Route configuration lives in `src/routes/index.ts` and maps URLs to page modules plus optional `loadData` hooks.
+- State management is Redux Toolkit based and is initialized from `src/store/`.
+- Client bootstraps live under `src/client/` with separate entry files for desktop and China variants.
+
+## Runtime variants
+
+- Default web app via `yarn dev`
+- Desktop flavor via `yarn dev-desktop`
+- China builds via `yarn dev-china` and `yarn dev-china-desktop`
+- Whitelabel builds via `yarn dev-whitelabel` and `yarn dev-whitelabel-desktop`
+
+## Server responsibilities
+
+- Security middleware such as `helmet` and `hpp`
+- Static asset serving from `public/`
+- Proxy helpers under `/proxy`, `/myproxy`, and `/chinaproxy`
+- SSR rendering
+- Cache invalidation hooks and cron initialization
+
+## Build and test
+
+- Webpack configs live in `webpack/`
+- Babel config is in `babel.config.js`
+- Jest config is in `jest/config.js`
+- Style and lint rules are configured in repo root dotfiles
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Code: src/server/index.ts
+- Code: src/server/ssr.tsx
+- Code: src/client/index.tsx
+- Code: src/client/indexDesktop.tsx
+- Code: src/store/index.ts
+- Code: jest/config.js
+
+## Related pages
+
+- [Overview](./Overview.md)
+- [Routes and Areas](./Routes-and-Areas.md)
+- [Operations](./Operations.md)
